00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:41.230
Dubai is a very different place from any other
in the Persian Gulf.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:46.590
Its economy isn’t based on oil, natural
gas or any other raw material, but instead,

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:49.900
mainly on tourism, transport, trade and finance.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.060
But despite not being rich in natural resources,
in the last four decades, Dubai became one

00:00:54.060 --> 00:01:03.690
of the most prosperous cities in history.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:07.869
Since the first towers began to emerge in
the desert, this city’s growth has been

00:01:07.869 --> 00:01:08.869
nonstop.

00:01:08.869 --> 00:01:12.900
The tallest building in the world, the largest
shopping mall, the largest airport, the most

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.479
luxurious hotel.

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:15.939
You can find everything here.

00:01:15.939 --> 00:01:20.009
And, well, we could say that this city is
made by and for money.

00:01:20.009 --> 00:01:25.810
Everything, absolutely everything in this
enclave is shaped by the money flowing in-to

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:26.939
and out-of it.

00:01:26.939 --> 00:01:34.969
However, 2018 hasn’t exactly been this emirate’s
happiest year.

00:01:34.969 --> 00:01:40.679
In the last 12 months, the Dubai stock market
has plummeted by almost 25%, new business

00:01:40.679 --> 00:01:52.270
licenses have decreased, and for the first
time ever, employment has also fallen.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:59.060
Today more and more analysts are wondering
whether Dubai is about to undergo a huge crisis.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:01.520
And this is, precisely, the main question.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.380
Will Dubai be losing its shine?

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:10.920
Listen up.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:15.940
(SIGNS AND SHADOWS)

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.770
While much of the Arab world is facing a great
deal of chaos, economic crises, political

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.750
crises, violence...

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:26.250
Dubai is very busy developing 3D printers,
theme parks, air taxi services and even working

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.560
to send a probe to Mars within just 3 years.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:35.820
But, as I was saying, 2018 hasn’t been a
very good year.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:40.350
Look, even though more than 90% of Dubai’s
population is foreign, schools for expatriates

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.600
are closing or losing students.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:47.640
Moving companies show one clear trend: more
people are leaving than arriving.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:51.440
And although the construction pace is still
in full swing, it’s becoming increasingly

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.080
clear that many of these new buildings are
half empty

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.510
Apartments, offices, hotels, shopping centers...

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:02.480
Obtaining official statistics isn’t easy,
but what happens when there’s more supply

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:03.480
than demand?

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.480
Prices drop, right?

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:13.930
Well that’s precisely what’s happening.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:17.490
And not only that, Emaar Properties’ stocks
– the company that built the Burj Khalifa

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:21.990
– and those of other large developers listed
on the Dubai stock exchange have suffered

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:25.690
a collapse of almost 40% in the last year.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:26.960
Want more?

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:31.870
Well, DXB Entertainments, the company that
owns most of the theme parks that have opened

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:36.151
in Dubai in recent years, such as Legoland
Dubai, MotionGate, and Bollywood Park, is

00:03:36.151 --> 00:03:41.380
negotiating with banks to restructure more
than one billion dollars in debt, simply because

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:44.150
the number of visitors is much lower than
expected.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:48.000
You can see that it isn’t exactly time to
celebrate.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:54.590
Now the question we can ask ourselves here,
on VisualPolitik is “what the hell is happening”?

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:57.380
Why is Dubai facing this possible crisis?

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:03.930
Is this the end of the emirate that has broken
every Middle Eastern mold?

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:09.320
Let's see.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:14.730
(THE STORM)

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.940
Dubai is facing a completely new scenario.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:22.200
In this case, the origin of its problem may
lie far beyond its rulers’ competence.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.430
Allow me to explain:

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:29.250
Dubai is perhaps the most famous emirate in
the United Arab Emirates, but it’s Abu Dhabi

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:31.620
that has the oil, money and power.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:36.780
In fact, even though Sheikh Mohammed bin Rashid
governs Dubai, it’s this man here, Muhammad

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:43.370
bin Zayed, the crown prince of Abu Dhabi,
who de facto rules all the United Arab Emirates.

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:48.940
Well, the key to Dubai’s huge success was
becoming something like the Switzerland of

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:53.150
the Middle East: the freest space, with the
most legal security, and the one most open

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:55.430
to the rest of the planet.

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:57.000
And, of course, low taxes.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:04.390
However, now some of these things are being
questioned.

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:08.630
In the last two to three years, the United
Arab Emirates government has adopted a very

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:10.240
active foreign policy.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:14.410
Prince Mohammad bin Zayed has completely aligned
himself with the Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:18.389
bin Salman, especially on two fronts: Qatar
and Iran.

00:05:18.389 --> 00:05:21.710
Check this out.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:25.990
On the one hand both countries have led the
blockade against Qatar, a country that had

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:27.890
very close ties with Dubai.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:31.810
In fact many international companies settled
in Dubai and their executives traveled to

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.010
and from Doha;

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:39.020
And Jebel Ali, Dubai’s great port, was also
Qatar’s most important supply center.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.560
Now that’s all over.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:44.950
With the blockade, the UAE ordered all Qatari
citizens to leave the country, most flights

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:47.450
were suspended, and freight traffic was interrupted.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:55.280
Now Qatar is directly provisioned by or through
Oman, but no longer through Jebel Ali.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:58.590
With the blockade Dubai has lost a very important
commercial partner.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:02.460
In addition to all this, many companies and
many investors have noticed that legal security

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:06.110
and maneuverability weren’t as strong as
they previously thought, because, as you can

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:09.780
see, Dubai ultimately depends on decisions
made in Abu Dhabi.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:18.760
But that’s not all.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:21.520
Dubai also had very important relations with
Iran.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:25.560
In fact, thanks to its proximity, Dubai became
something of an escape route, a place for

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:30.290
many Iranian leaders and entrepreneurs to
stay for a few days, have fun and spend some

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:31.290
money.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:34.820
And not only that, every year their commercial
business transactions with Iran surpassed

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:36.400
20 billion dollars.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:40.680
But now, because of US sanctions and the growing
diplomatic conflict between Riyadh and Tehran,

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:43.300
this trade is shrinking by leaps and bounds.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:46.690
The ships that used to send goods every week
now go once a month.

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:53.050
In other words, in just over a year, Dubai
has lost two of its largest trading partners,

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.150
due to decisions made in Abu Dhabi.

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:59.370
And, do you think that’s all?

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:00.370
Well...

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:02.190
It’s definitely not.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:06.190
Just as Dubai became a sort of playground
and second safe zone for Iranians, the same

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.020
thing happened with Saudi citizens and businessmen.

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:10.020
Of course!

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:13.960
Given all the restrictions that Saudi Arabia
has, for the Saudis, Dubai is an oasis of

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.169
freedom and safety.

00:07:15.169 --> 00:07:19.470
Well, when the Saudi prince, Mohammed Bin
Salman unleashed his war against “corruption”

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:24.490
- or a move to consolidate his power - and
locked up or kidnapped dozens of Saudi businessmen

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:29.410
and senior officials, the Arab Emirates Central
Bank demanded all banks operating in the country

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:33.090
to give Riyadh all the information they had
on the detainees’ accounts.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:37.700
And they delivered all this information even
when they hadn’t been charged; information

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:42.090
that, of course, Riyadh used to get money
from all the businessmen who had to buy their

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:43.100
freedom with their checkbooks.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:49.500
That way, the Saudi businessmen who thought
that Dubai was the true Switzerland of the

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:53.169
Middle East realized that this wasn’t quite
so.

00:07:53.169 --> 00:07:57.680
Yes, in Dubai there’s legal security and
your savings are safe, but not the information

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:00.510
with which the autocratic Saudi government
can extort you.

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:04.650
Do you see where the problem is?

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:09.169
Well, due to these reasons, and others, the
Dubai financial industry is also suffering.

00:08:09.169 --> 00:08:15.419
But no, we haven’t yet reached the end of
the list, the headaches don’t stop here.

00:08:15.419 --> 00:08:20.280
The dropping oil prices in recent years have
affected the purchasing power of many of the

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:22.190
people who spend their money in Dubai.

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:26.600
A lower oil price means less income and that,
as we’ve seen here on VisualPolitik, has

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:31.080
meant that some countries like Saudi Arabia
have had to make many, many cuts.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:36.800
And, finally, there’s another factor that
depends on Dubai itself: in a certain way,

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:40.020
the city runs the risk of becoming a victim
of its own success.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:44.850
Yes, you heard that right.

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:50.400
Thanks to Dubai’s huge success, its prices
have skyrocketed, especially real estate prices.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:55.640
And Dubai has very low taxes, but the state
gets many resources through building licenses...

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:56.920
which hasn’t helped either.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:00.480
If to all of this, we add the fact that many
Middle Eastern countries, to reduce their

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.150
dependence on oil, have launched plans to
copy this city by giving many advantages to

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:09.040
their investors... the result is that Dubai
has lost its appeal to international companies

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:10.070
in recent years.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:13.580
Anyway, as you now see, these are the roots
of the problem:

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:14.700
Abu Dhabi
Qatar

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:17.890
Iran
And the cost of its own success has decreased

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:20.950
this emirate city’s attractive oasis status.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:27.330
But what many of you may be wondering is,
what now?

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:33.470
Listen up.

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:36.540
(PERSPECTIVES)

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:41.321
Even though its economy is expected to grow
by just over 2% in 2019, as you can see, Dubai

00:09:41.321 --> 00:09:43.570
isn’t going through the best of times.

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:49.480
But, just a second, this doesn’t mean everything
is lost, not at all.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:53.440
In spite of everything, this city-emirate
continues to be an oasis in the desert and

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.960
its government seems to have a clear idea
of the keys to its success.

00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:00.850
Therefore, what Sheikh Mohammed bin Rashid’s
government is doing now, is trying to make

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:04.920
Dubai's economy even more competitive with
its neighbors: to do so, they are making it

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:08.770
easier to obtain a VISA, they’re ensuring
that expatriates who lose their jobs have

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:13.580
an easier time staying, and they are decreasing
the obstacles of foreign business owners outside

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:17.250
the special economic zones.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:21.130
In other words, they want to connect Dubai
even more to the rest of the world.

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:25.100
In fact, local authorities have high hopes
for the arrival of Chinese investors.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:28.120
(“This is a market cycle that we have to
accept.

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:32.020
The government is doing what it did in past
slumps, sitting down with business to figure

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:33.180
out solutions".

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:38.480
Fahad Al Gergawi, head of investment agency
Dubai FDI.)

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:44.060
("When the upturn does arrive, Dubai’s companies
will emerge leaner and more competitive”.

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:49.010
Khatija Haque, head of regional research at
local lender Emirates NBD)

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:54.730
Folks, this is what’s happening in this
city-state that has had such a positive influence

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:55.730
on the entire Middle East.

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:59.890
Yes, in Dubai, a lot of unfortunate things
may be reported, but opening up to the world

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:04.510
has been a breath of fresh air for one of
the most hostile areas on the planet in terms

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:05.510
of human rights.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:10.279
In Dubai, not only can you drink alcohol,
eat pork, and pray at a Catholic church, now

00:11:10.279 --> 00:11:13.680
you can even go to a Synagogue and eat Kosher
food.

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:16.420
Yes, you heard that right.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:20.270
( “As the Gulf Warms Up to Israel, a Synagogue
Grows in Dubai”.

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:21.270
Bloomberg)

00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:25.100
Anyway, only the future will be able to tell
if this city-state’s frenetic growth pace

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:30.959
will continue or if instead Dubai is doomed
to suffer a huge crisis and lose its shine.

00:11:30.959 --> 00:11:33.060
So far, the party continues:

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:38.270
(A Dubai company will build the largest sports
shopping center in the world, The Gulf Post)

